course: dictionary
lesson: 6802
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Organisation is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «A charity is an organisation that helps people, animals or the environment.» Here an organisation is a group of people working together for a purpose.
explain: Look at the clues. «Hurting animals on purpose is cruelty; tell a trusted adult, who can report it to an animal welfare organisation.» The sentence is about helping animals, so an organisation here is a group that works to protect them.
explain: The other meanings are about arranging things. Organisation can mean how things are arranged or planned, or being able to keep things in order. Packing your bag and planning your homework are both organisation.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «A promotion is a move up to a more senior job in the same organisation.» Does "a group of people who work together" fit? Yes, it does, so that is the right meaning.
fact: An organisation is a group of people who work together for a purpose.
fact: Organisation can also mean how things are arranged or planned, or being able to keep things in order.
fact: «A charity is an organisation that helps people, animals or the environment.»
fact: Charities, clubs, companies, schools and the United Nations are all examples of organisations.
fact: In writing, organisation means putting your ideas in a clear order, with paragraphs.
exercise: «A charity is an organisation that helps people, animals or the environment.» What is an organisation in this sentence? | A type of bag | A kind of weather | A single person working alone | *A group of people who work together for a purpose
exercise: Which describes good organisation? | Doing nothing at all | Losing your pencil case every day | *Keeping things in order and planning ahead | Shouting loudly in class
exercise: Which of these is an example of an organisation? | A sunny day | A sharpened pencil | A whisper | *The Red Cross
test: «Hurting animals on purpose is cruelty; tell a trusted adult, who can report it to an animal welfare organisation.» In this sentence, what does organisation mean? | How a school bag is packed | *A group that works to protect animals | A kind of animal | A quiet place to sit
test: In writing, what does organisation mean? | A list of who is in your class | Drawing a picture to go with your story | *Putting ideas in a clear order, with paragraphs | Writing in very large letters
exam: «That is why people argue: about more money or better organisation, about public or private help, about who pays which share.» In this sentence, what does organisation mean? | *The way things are arranged or planned | A bird that lives in the trees | A quiet voice | A charity that helps animals
